---
title: "resultsPublicationFlow (High Level Sale Customer Journey)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_refund_ended: Legion initiates results publication
    q_check_refund_ended --> q_check_sale_type: block.timestamp > refundEndTime
    q_check_refund_ended --> q_revert_early: refund period not ended
    q_revert_early --> [*]: revert RefundPeriodActive
    q_check_sale_type --> q_fixed_publish: saleType = FixedPrice OR OpenApplication
    q_check_sale_type --> q_sealed_init: saleType = SealedBidAuction
    q_check_sale_type --> q_pre_liquid_publish: saleType = PreLiquidApproved
    q_sealed_init --> q_lock_cancel: initializePublishSaleResults()
    q_lock_cancel --> q_set_private_key: cancelLocked = true
    q_set_private_key --> q_publish_merkle: publishSaleResults(merkleRoot, capitalRaised, privateKey)
    q_fixed_publish --> q_publish_merkle: publishSaleResults(merkleRoot, capitalRaised)
    q_pre_liquid_publish --> q_publish_tge: publishTgeDetails(askToken, supply, allocations)
    q_publish_tge --> q_publish_raised: publishRaisedCapital(capitalRaised)
    q_publish_raised --> q_set_merkle: set allocation Merkle roots
    q_publish_merkle --> q_set_merkle: set allocation Merkle roots
    q_set_merkle --> q_set_accepted: setAcceptedCapital(merkleRoot)
    q_set_accepted --> [*]: results published, claims enabled

    note right of q_lock_cancel
        INV-001: Results publication only after refund period ends
        INV-002: For sealed bids, cancellation is locked before results are published
        INV-003: Merkle roots enable trustless verification of allocations
        INV-004: Only Legion operators can publish results
    end note
